 "readme": {
  "file": "README.md",
  "title": "Constructive Cryptography on Random Systems",
  "excerpt": "This repository formalizes Constructive Cryptography [1, 2] in Lean 4. The framework is instantiated on a theory of random systems [3, 4] in which a system answers exactly on a declared domain of input histories, and a converter may stop at random. The classes of the framework are assumptions; their instances on interfaces take every field from the typed systems and typed converters of the random-systems library. The algebra of typed systems and converters is also stated in category-theoretic terms; a categorical model of composable security is given in [7]."
 },
